== Trivia ==
* [[anti:Birthright|Birthright]] is from the ''Antibirth'' mod.
** Before ''Antibirth'' the item originated from the ''Binding of Isaac: Community Remix'' mod, where it was known as 'Soul Script'.
* This item's name, description, and unlock requirement are a reference to the biblical story of Jacob and Esau, in which Esau trades his birthrights to Jacob in exchange for [[Red Stew|stew]].
** When {{c|Tainted Jacob}} picks up Birthright, {{e|Dark Esau}}, a representation of his own rage, seemingly becomes only angrier and doubles in power.
*** Birthright's effect doubling Dark Esau's power, instead of Tainted Jacob's, and the quote "it's not yours", further reflects the fact that it was originally his.
* Prior to patch [[V1.7.6]], Tainted Jacob's Birthright pickup quote was "''There is no escape''".
* {{c|Tainted Keeper}}'s pickup quote could be based off the song ''Money, Money, Money'', by the band ABBA.
* {{c|Eden}}'s Birthright could be a reference to how Eden functions in the card game ''The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls,'' as Eden starts the game by drawing 3 treasure cards and selecting one to keep permanently while the other two are discarded.

